NTP (old)

Synchronizes clocks between systems communicating over a packet-switched, variable-latency data network

Sent over UDP using port 123

How it works

Stratum 0 - 15

0 = Most precise timekeeping devices
1 (Primary time servers) = Any computer whose system time is synchronized within a few microseconds of an attached stratum ZERO device
2 = Any computer whose system time is synchronized within a few microseconds of an attached stratum ONE device or queried to multiple stratum ONE servers
3 = Same but connecting to straum 2 servers
4 ... Same ( Each time adds more delay )

Newer Protocol fixing weaknesses

Precision Time Protocol (PTP) - Synchronizes clocks throughoout a computer network offering a higher precision solution for scenarios where every microsecond counts
Network Time Security Protocol (NTS) - Extension of NTP providing cryptographic security 